import json,statistics
from pathlib import Path
import matplotlib
matplotlib.use('Agg')
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
p=Path('results/mnist_masked_gate_refinement_20261106');r=json.loads((p/'results.json').read_text());t=json.loads((p/'test_results.json').read_text());selected=json.loads((p/'selection.json').read_text());lines=['# Masked-decoder branch-gate refinement','', '18 sequential-training runs: three seeds × two task orders × three decoder-training variants. Original sparse168x4 MLP with hybrid5 classification+auxiliary training, two epochs/task. No replay. A small 168→32 tanh→784 sigmoid decoder adds31,280 parameters (125,120 bytes float32), total165,354 parameters. No skip connections from pixels to decoder output.','', '| Decoder training | Validation: 0 steps | 1 step | 5 steps | 10 steps |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for arm in ['decoder_only','joint_0.1','joint_1.0']:
 rr=[a for a in r if a['arm']==arm];cells=[f"{100*statistics.mean(a['validation'][str(s)]['accuracy'] for a in rr):.2f}%" for s in [0,1,5,10]];lines.append('| '+arm+' | '+' | '.join(cells)+' |')
lines+=['',f"Validation selected **{selected['arm']}, {selected['steps']} refinement steps**. This is the unchanged image-only classifier, so the candidate did not beat the baseline.",'', '## Test curve for the validation-selected decoder arm','', '| Gate-refinement steps | Classification accuracy | Masked reconstruction error | Corrected images | Newly wrong images |','|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|'];values=[]
for step in [0,1,5,10]:
 v=[statistics.mean(a['scores'][str(step)]['accuracy']*100 for a in t if a['seed']==s) for s in [101,102,103]];mse=statistics.mean(a['scores'][str(step)]['reconstruction_mse'] for a in t);corrected=statistics.mean(a['scores'][str(step)]['corrected'] for a in t);harmed=statistics.mean(a['scores'][str(step)]['harmed'] for a in t);values.append(dict(steps=step,accuracy=statistics.mean(v),seed_sd=statistics.stdev(v),mse=mse));lines.append(f'| {step} | {statistics.mean(v):.2f} ± {statistics.stdev(v):.2f}% | {mse:.4f} | {corrected:.1f} | {harmed:.1f} |')
lines+=['','Corrected/newly-wrong counts average six 10,000-image evaluations relative to step0. These reused queries are not independent datasets. Accuracy SD uses three seed-level averages over training orders. All test curve steps were prespecified; step selection uses validation only.','', '## Procedure','', 'Classifier training remains the original hybrid5 objective on full images. A second masked-image forward pass predicts30% missing pixels through the current trace-selected hidden representation. Reconstruction loss uses masked pixels only with foreground weighting1+4×raw target intensity. decoder_only detaches hidden features, so classifier parameters/trajectories remain the original baseline. joint_0.1 and joint_1.0 backpropagate weighted reconstruction loss into branch weights. Original classifier and decoder gradients clipped separately; Adam .0005, batch128. Decoder is trained on each current task only and may itself forget.','', 'Inference freezes every parameter and training trace. Each image independently initializes gate logits from its full-image branch-response magnitudes. Four deterministic masked views provide reconstruction targets, using only that image’s pixels, no labels. Adam .1 updates only the image’s168×4 gate logits, minimizing masked MSE plus .01 KL to initial weights. Classification reads the full image with the adapted gates. Gates reset for each image; no task grouping, support labels, route archive or temporal context is used. Model tensors are asserted unchanged.','', '## Interpretation','', 'Reconstruction quality is not an adequate classifier-verification signal in this experiment: optimizing it can move gates away from correct labels. Joint training changes that tradeoff but does not improve validation over the current baseline. This does not establish that every generative/predictive inference mechanism fails. It does not isolate whether decoder forgetting, task-insensitive pixel loss, gate/decoder mismatch or other objective issues dominate. No stronger class-conditioned decoder or feature-based prediction objective was tested.','', 'Fixed recipes and masks were specified before querying results; the model/benchmark has been explored previously. No definitive reasoning claim follows from this experiment. Two tests passed: visible-pixel targets do not affect masked loss, and refinement preserves all model tensors while step0 reproduces current classifier predictions.']
(p/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');(p/'summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(values,indent=2))
fig,axs=plt.subplots(1,2,figsize=(10,4));steps=[a['steps'] for a in values];axs[0].errorbar(steps,[a['accuracy'] for a in values],yerr=[a['seed_sd'] for a in values],marker='o',capsize=3);axs[0].set_ylabel('Test classification accuracy (%)');axs[1].plot(steps,[a['mse'] for a in values],marker='o',color='#b45309');axs[1].set_ylabel('Masked reconstruction error (lower is better)')
for ax in axs:ax.set_xlabel('Per-image gate-refinement steps');ax.set_xticks(steps);ax.grid(alpha=.2)
fig.suptitle('Better reconstruction did not produce better classification');fig.tight_layout();fig.savefig(p/'reconstruction_vs_classification.png',dpi=180);plt.close(fig)
print('\n'.join(lines[:21]))
